            description: "UNH evaluated Canadice as a seedless table grape in Durham, New Hampshire. Fruit color: red. 2016-2019 ratings: anthracnose low, downy mildew low, powdery mildew low, vigor high. Fruit notes: Tight, very attractive and uniform clusters. Trial notes: 2019 preliminary results say Mars and Canadice produced more marketable fruit than all other varieties. Source conclusion: UNH preliminary conclusions identify Mars and Canadice as most promising for commercial production of seedless table grapes in the region"
